# Shell scripts must keep LF endings even on a Windows checkout with
# core.autocrlf=true. A CRLF shebang makes the kernel look for an interpreter
# named "/bin/bash\r", and the container reports it as
# "cannot execute: required file not found" - which looks like a missing file,
# not a line-ending problem. The failure is silent at the layer that matters:
# postgres still reports healthy, and the only symptom is the API failing later
# with "database mem0_app does not exist".
*.sh text eol=lf
